  "measurement_note": "Size S is n, the number of array elements, and k = S/2. Legal tiers 24, 96, and 384 span 16x. A repeated six-value pattern keeps a nontrivial GCD and has exactly enough minimum-exponent elements to double the full-subarray GCD, so incremental GCD and exponent-count maintenance remain active. The accepted enumeration is O(n^2 log M). A correct calibrated alternative recomputes each subarray's GCD and minimum-exponent count from scratch in O(n^3 log M) and must fail only scaling.",
